{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>For it is your reward, etc., in exchange, etc.</b> He returned to state the very same things he said above, because he said <b>and you shall eat it in every place</b> — which is completely unconsecrated. Therefore he gave the reason: for there is in this tithe no sanctity at all like terumah or similar to it, but rather profane property that HaShem told Israel to pay to you as the wage for your service. From now on, what sanctity is in it?" "And our Rabbis of blessed memory (Sifrei Numbers 122) said that the verse comes to say that if he served he receives, and if he did not serve he does not receive. From here they said: a Levite who accepted upon himself all the services except for one has no share in the Levitical gifts. And both these and those are words of the living Elohim." "<b>Thus concludes the portion of Korah.</b>"], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:54.881593849Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}